# Navigation typing

These rules are **blocking**. Any violation MUST be fixed before merge.

## Single source of truth

- All React Navigation param lists, navigator props types, and related route/type aliases for the app MUST be defined in `src/navigation/types.ts` (or explicitly exported from that file as the canonical definitions).
- Screens, navigators, hooks, and shared utilities MUST NOT define inline or local duplicates of navigation param types (for example `type RootStackParamList = { ... }` outside `src/navigation/types.ts`).
- Screens, navigators, and hooks MUST import navigation types from `src/navigation/types.ts` (or from a barrel that re-exports only those definitions) instead of re-declaring equivalent types.

## Reuse

- The same route names and param object shapes MUST use the **same** types from `src/navigation/types.ts` everywhere: stack/tab/screen components, `useNavigation`, `RouteProp`, `NativeStackScreenProps`, and custom hooks that touch navigation.
- Adding a new route or changing params MUST be done by updating `src/navigation/types.ts` first; consumers MUST be updated to use the shared types only.

Violations (local param list types, duplicated route typings, or screens typed without the central definitions) are blocking issues and MUST be corrected before merge.
